{"t": 1794112373.7515023, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f Regression flagged: this change replaced rounding with `int()` truncation in `worker/rates.py`, which drops fractions instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. It is causing a production reconciliation mismatch (expected 1100, got 1099).\n\nSentry error: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 `ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit`, 2,201 events, first seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, suspect commit `8c2f1d0` (this PR).\n\nFix: restore rounding in `convert()` (`round(amount_minor * rate)`).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
